                "retweet_count": 7,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today, the Supreme Court rightly ruled in Medina v. Planned Parenthood South Atlantic that the Medicaid statute does not create a federal right to choose a specific provider, and that South Carolina has the right to exclude Planned Parenthood from Medicaid. This decision respects the constitutional role of Congress and ensures that disputes over state Medicaid decisions are handled through the proper channels and not through activist litigation.",
